senses.gloss:
nikāya,
(1) (as in Skt., but nt., in Skt. m.) collection, group: yena … deva-nikāyaṃ tenopasaṃkrameyaṃ Mv 〔i.54.13〕; Buddha is saptabhiś ca nikāyaiḥ saṃpuraskṛto Divy 〔159.15〕;
(2) (= Pali id.) ‘collection’ of sūtras in the Buddhist canon, or more loosely, the canon collectively: nikāya-gati-saṃbhavāt Laṅk 〔292.13〕, from (having their) origin in the course of the canon, and ˚gati-gotrā(ḥ) 16, said of the abhijñā (psychic powers, Suzuki) as acquired by orthodox canonical lore; Suzuki misunderstands the mg., which is made clear by naikāyika, q.v., shortly after;
(3) school (of religious opinion), in nikāyāntarīya, q.v. (orig. and lit., no doubt, canon as under 2). The four Nikāyas of the Pali canon are usually called Āgamas in BHS.

nikṣipati,
(1) figures, calculates, works out (a mathematical problem): LV 〔146.12, 15, 16, 20, 22〕; 〔147.2〕; see s.v. uddiśati;
(2) lets down in sense of permits to descend: LV 〔186.13 f.〕 (see s.v. utkṣipati, 1); Tib. ḥbebs, cause to descend.
